      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 1890s, Milwaukee elites Jacob Donges and Frederick Usinger built summer homes in the Fairy Chasm community near the lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayside%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The stone Lion’s Gates, erected in 1911 at Lake Drive and Fairy Chasm Road, still mark the original Donges and Usinger estates.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.baysidewi.gov/community/history.php",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Uihlein family, owners of the Joseph Schlitz Brewing Company, purchased land in 1885 that became Nine Mile Farm, where draft horses were bred for the brewery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayside%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1969, a debate over the Schlitz Foundation’s land sparked a community decision to preserve the area as public space, leading to the Schlitz Audubon Nature Center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
